<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hispano-Moroccan War (1859–1860)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1859">1859</a>–<a href="/years/1860">1860</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Spanish-Moroccan War, War of Africa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hispano-Moroccan War was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> from October 1859 to April 1860, after attacks on the Spanish enclave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a>. A Spanish army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopoldo-odonnell">Leopoldo O'Donnell</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tetouan">Tetouan</a> in February 1860 and won at Wad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras">Ras</a> in March. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-wad-ras">Treaty of Wad Ras</a> enlarged Ceuta, imposed an indemnity and promised Spain a coastal territory later identified as Ifni.</p></div>
